        "position": 3,
        "title": "Finally found the right design!",
        "text": "I’ve looked (now and then) for decades for an ideal tick removal tweezers design and finally found it! These are perfect! You want to be able to firmly grasp the tick tightly against the skin with the compression force as far forward on the tick’s body as possible to minimize injection of fluids in the tick into you by squeezing it.The height of the compression surface is on the order of a half mm or a little less with the rest of the tips angled away so as not to squeeze the tick further off the skin.The finishing of the pair I got was quite good, though I did a tiny bit of touch up with a jewelers’ file on a couple of sharp edges. They’re also plenty strong.Don’t forget: testing the tick for pathogens works about a thousand times better than testing the bitten person, so save the tick in a Ziplock bag so you can send it to a lab that’s a good choice for your circumstances.",
